      "parity": "match",
      "notes": "stored[ticket=N] selects the stored trade with that ticket. stored[*] = every stored trade; value {anyOf: [...]} = equals one of the listed values; line 52 asserts each listed Double isFinite. Row 3 (unbalanced quote) yields too few fields and is skipped. Row 4 starts with a non-digit, which ENDS the trade section (break, not skip), so row 5 (ticket overflow) is never read. Sanitizing: non-finite metrics (nan, +inf, -inf) become 0, NOT the +/-1e9 limit; finite metrics clamp to +/-1e9; lots non-finite -> 0, else min(|lots|, 1e6); durations clamp to [0, 5_270_400] (10 x 366 days in minutes); an hour outside 0-23 is replaced by the open time's UTC hour; an invalid day by the open time's UTC weekday (EEE, en_US_POSIX); closeTime < openTime -> closeTime = openTime; symbol: control characters removed, trimmed, first 32 characters. The comment's CSV quotes are toggled away by parseCSVLine. Decimal fields from \"inf\"/\"1e300\" (beyond Decimal's range) are not derived."
